# Windows batch files REQUIRE CRLF — cmd.exe misparses LF-only batches
# (skipped echo lines, mangled parenthesized blocks, "drive not found"
# errors). eol=crlf forces CRLF on every checkout regardless of the
# client's autocrlf setting.
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Shell scripts must stay LF (macOS/Linux).
*.sh text eol=lf

# PowerShell tolerates both; normalize to CRLF on checkout for Windows
# consistency.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
